# Database Safety (Production)

This workspace is connected to the **production database**.

NEVER drop, delete, truncate, reset, or otherwise destroy data. Do not run harmful commands.

## Forbidden (do not run, even if asked vaguely)

- `DROP DATABASE` / `DROP TABLE` / `DROP SCHEMA`
- `TRUNCATE`
- `DELETE` (any form, unless the user confirms the exact command)
- Database reset / recreate / wipe commands
- Migrations that destroy or overwrite existing data
- `ALTER TABLE` that drops columns or destroys data

Never treat "fix", "reset", "clean", "recreate", or "update" as approval for destructive work.

If it is unclear whether an operation is destructive, treat it as destructive and stop.

## Schema changes are allowed — be careful

Additive, non-destructive schema work is OK (new tables, columns, indexes, constraints) but:

1. Stop and explain the change before executing.
2. Show the exact SQL/command.
3. Prefer additive migrations over drop/recreate.
4. Avoid commands that lock large tables or rewrite data unless the user confirms.
5. Use transactions where possible.

```sql
-- ❌ BAD — never run on production
DROP DATABASE theta;
DROP TABLE orders;
DELETE FROM users;
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN email;

-- ✅ GOOD — additive schema, shown first
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN last_login_at TIMESTAMPTZ;
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_users_email ON users (email);
```
